<title>POLAND: PPWK plans share buy-up or payout.</title>
<headline>PPWK plans share buy-up or payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polskie Przedsiebiorstwo Wydawnictw Kartograficznych SA (PPWK) plans to earmark 20 percent of its 1996 net profit for buying up its shares to retire them or for a dividend, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>PPWK, which had a net profit of 4.4 million zlotys in 1996, said in a Thursday's statement the dividend would be at 0.25 zlotys per share.</p>
<p>It said the final decision would be taken by its general shareholders meeting on April 25.</p>
<p>Last year PPWK paid a dividend of 0.5 zlotys per share.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
